      "final_text": "Done \u2014 `check_candidate` returns `VERIFIED` and `verify_passport` reproduces it.\n\n**Fix:** [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean) now defines `VyperSqrt.sqrt` as the deployed loop with the PR-4486 correction \u2014 `vyperSqrtWith (fun y z => if y < z then y else z)`, i.e. the min of the last two iterates instead of the last iterate. That turns the sometimes-rounded-up result into the floor of the root.\n\n**Proofs:** all 5 required theorems proved with the exact locked statements, no `sorry`:\n- A Nat model (`AN`, `sN`, `z0N`, `seqN`) mirrors the loop as Newton iteration `newton A x = (x + A/x)/2`, using `ProofForgeFin.Sqrt` single-step lemmas.\n- Seed bound `s \u2264 z0`, overflow bound `A/z + z \u2264 2^167-1`, halving convergence `e\u2096 \u2264 2^(167-k)+2`, so after 167 steps the error is \u2264 3 and one quadratic step lands in `{s, s+1}`; the loop's final pair has min `s`.\n- `REQ-SQRT-NOT-ABOVE` / `NOT-BELOW` follow from `s*s \u2264 A < (s+1)*(s+1)` transferred to `Int`; `TOTAL` from the loop always returning `some`; `NEG-REVERTS` and `DEPLOYED-LOOP` directly from the definition.\n\n**Verification:** `lean_build` clean; `check_candidate` VERIFIED all 5 requirements across all six kernels with only permitted axioms, executable passing 2001 property cases; Passport `.proofforge/passport-001.json` (`e485e222\u2026bc2c92`) reproduced by `verify_passport`.",
